  "projects": {
    "2017": [
      {
        "title": "Enhancements collection for phpMyAdmin",
        "short_description": "The project aims at enhancing phpMyAdmin by implementing several features. The following is the list of enhancements:\nNew UI for Multi-table query...",
        "description": "<p>The project aims at enhancing phpMyAdmin by implementing several features. The following is the list of enhancements:\nNew UI for Multi-table query generator,\nDefault options for transformations,\nAllow designer to show other Databases, \nGoogle Authenticator,\nConsolidate tablesorter libraries, \nFacilitate drag and drop of columns between tables,\nSetup improvements.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Achilles-96",
        "code_url": "https://raghuramvadapalli.wordpress.com/2017/08/24/closing-gsoc-final-code-submission/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/6426335958269952/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Improving phpMyAdmin's Selenium testsuite and Error Reporting Server",
        "short_description": "phpMyAdmin has been around for more than eighteen years now. Over all these years, a variety of new features have been added to it. In wake of new...",
        "description": "<p>phpMyAdmin has been around for more than eighteen years now. Over all these years, a variety of new features have been added to it. In wake of new features being implemented and the existing bugs being fixed, it becomes increasingly important to not break existing functionality of commonly used features. Although, unit testing helps in preventing some of breakages, a consistent and robust selenium test-suite is as imperative to ascertain that none of the commonly used flows are broken.</p>\n<p>This project aims to <strong>fix the project’s currently broken selenium testing</strong>, so that the complete suite can be run on every commit and also <strong>add to the existing set of tests to cover more features and related flows</strong>.</p>\n<p>Additionally, it also <strong>involves improving phpMyAdmin’s error reporting server by implementing a set of new features</strong>, that would be useful for the developers in maintaining the project better.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Deven Bansod",
        "code_url": "https://devenbansod.wordpress.com/2017/08/26/google-summer-of-code-17-with-phpmyadmin-summary/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/6246403672113152/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Enhancements collection",
        "short_description": "phpmyadmin currently has a large number of open issues (~210 at time of writing this). To maintain and improve phpmyadmin core project the numbers of...",
        "description": "<p>phpmyadmin currently has a large number of open issues (~210 at time of writing this). To maintain and improve phpmyadmin core project the numbers of issues should be lower down. This project aims to resolving the major issues and improvements to be done in phpmyadmin. I have selected a list of issues on which I will be working this summer.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "manishbisht",
        "code_url": "https://goo.gl/wHfQjS",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2017/projects/4854940837085184/"
      }
    ],
    "2018": [
      {
        "title": "Leonardo Strozzi's Application",
        "short_description": "I'm Leonardo Strozzi, a 19 year old, studying computer science, applying a proposal for the 'Refactoring Twig Templates' phpMyAdmin GSoC idea. The...",
        "description": "<p>I'm Leonardo Strozzi, a 19 year old, studying computer science, applying a proposal for the 'Refactoring Twig Templates' phpMyAdmin GSoC idea. The general idea of the project is to improve the in use Twig Templates, and replace some php functions to Twig features. There's also plenty of room for the inheritance and block features, replacing some of the current includes.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Strozzi",
        "code_url": "https://medium.com/@leo.strozzi98/gsoc-2018-contributions-documentation-1e0a3e0391d3",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/5697070107197440/"
      },
      {
        "title": "General Improvements",
        "short_description": "The aim of the project is to implement some of the enhancements suggested in the issue tracker to improve user experience(adding new useful features...",
        "description": "<p>The aim of the project is to implement some of the enhancements suggested in the issue tracker to improve user experience(adding new useful features and making the app easier to use), security and  performance.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Lakshya arora",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/nulll-pointer/6170d0746c0811b57e02827591e09365",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/5501169266851840/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Introducing modern JS features and tools",
        "short_description": "The javascript code is written in ES5 exposing many of the variables and functions globally and the package manager is not used for the modules.\nSo I...",
        "description": "<p>The javascript code is written in ES5 exposing many of the variables and functions globally and the package manager is not used for the modules.\nSo I will work on implementing package manager for modules like jQuery, jQplot etc which are being used in phpMyAdmin, transforming ES5 code to ES6 which has new features block scoped variable defining, classes and dynamic import-export, babel compiler for compiling ES6 code to ES5 which browsers support.\nThe functions will also be converted into modules which makes it easier to import the required function only. This will help in making the functions unit testable.\nI will also implement webpack which will bundle the static JavaScript files and also minify them, which can be loaded as scripts.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Piyush Vijay",
        "code_url": "https://medium.com/@piyush3079/gsoc-final-blog-for-code-submission-6ca7181f9d9e",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/6176165119131648/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Automated Theme Generator Tool",
        "short_description": "Currently there are pre-generated themes that can be manually installed and used. The idea is to create a tool that automates and makes easier the...",
        "description": "<p>Currently there are pre-generated themes that can be manually installed and used. The idea is to create a tool that automates and makes easier the task of creating themes. Themes created from the Theme Generator tool would be less prone to bugs in the long run and could cater to each individuals needs.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Saksham Gupta",
        "code_url": "https://medium.com/@shucon01/gsoc18-final-code-submission-7cb50aa5a8c6",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/6019213995016192/"
      }
    ],
    "2019": [
      {
        "title": "Refactoring and Improving Designer",
        "short_description": "When the designer section of phpMyAdmin was initially written, there was no jQuery. But now since it exists and due to the advantages of jQuery over...",
        "description": "<p>When the designer section of phpMyAdmin was initially written, there was no jQuery. But now since it exists and due to the advantages of jQuery over JavaScript and it’s a necessity over here, we could make this section better by making use of jQuery and also resolve the existing issues. Also, this project will be beneficial for both the important stakeholders, i.e. developers and user community.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Mohit Kuri",
        "code_url": "https://medium.com/@ikurimohit/gsoc-pma-final-submission-b93d47c53f5f",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/5626066008276992/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Convert UI to Bootstrap 4",
        "short_description": "Currently, the frontend of PMA is inconsistent and full of small issues. Its high time we switch from custom-written stylesheets to some more...",
        "description": "<p>Currently, the frontend of PMA is inconsistent and full of small issues. Its high time we switch from custom-written stylesheets to some more dependable and regularly updated framework. So this project aims to refactor the UI using Bootstrap 4.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Nupur Agrawal",
        "code_url": "https://pmagsocproject.wordpress.com/2019/08/25/gsoc-2019-final-work-summary/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/6066472223244288/"
      }
    ]
